------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Provenance
------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The encoder and decoder are original implementations written from the prose
and tables of RFC 6716 (Definition of the Opus Audio Codec) as updated by
RFC 8251, and from RFC 7845 (Ogg Encapsulation for Opus) for the
identification header and channel mappings. The reference implementation
attached to RFC 6716 as source code was not read, copied or translated, nor
was libopus, FFmpeg's Opus code or any other implementation. The SILK tables
were extracted from the RFC text by a script; the CELT constants the RFC's
prose names but does not list are written from the author's knowledge of the
specification and are verified by the official test vectors (see
docs/PROVENANCE.md).

The official Opus test vectors (opus_testvectors-rfc8251, published by the
Opus project and the IETF) are used as data only, downloaded at test time;
they are not part of this package. The SILK-to-48 kHz resampling filters in
src/resample_fit.rs were fitted by least squares to three of those vectors'
reference outputs (a black-box measurement of a non-normative component).

